{
  "slug": "adjetivos-posesivos",
  "number": 9,
  "part": 2,
  "level": "A1",
  "title": "Adjectives and possessives",
  "tagline": "Agreement, word order, mi / tu / su, and «es mío».",
  "goal": "Make adjectives agree with nouns, place them after the noun, use possessives (mi, tu, su, nuestro) and say whose something is.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "concordancia",
      "title": "Agreement",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Adjectives change to match the noun in **gender** and **number**:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Ending", "masc.", "fem.", "plural"],
          "rows": [
            ["**-o**", "*un gato negr{o}*", "*una gata negr{a}*", "*gatos negr{os}, gatas negr{as}*"],
            ["**-e**", "*un chico amabl{e}*", "*una chica amabl{e}*", "*chicos amabl{es}*"],
            ["**consonant**", "*un libro azul*", "*una casa azul*", "*casas azul{es}*"],
            ["**nationality**", "*inglés, español*", "*ingles{a}, español{a}*", "*ingleses, españolas*"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "posicion",
      "title": "Where the adjective goes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The opposite of English: most adjectives go **after** the noun. *una casa grande* (a big house), *el carro rojo* (the red car)."
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "items": [
            "Numbers and quantities go before: *dos perros, muchos amigos, poco tiempo*.",
            "*bueno* and *malo* often go before and shorten before a masculine noun: *un {buen} día, un {mal} momento*.",
            "*grande* before a noun becomes *gran* and means «great»: *un {gran} hombre* (a great man) vs *un hombre grande* (a big man)."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "posesivos",
      "title": "Possessives",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["English", "Before the noun", "After the noun / alone"],
          "rows": [
            ["my", "*mi, mis*", "*mío, mía, míos, mías*"],
            ["your (tú)", "*tu, tus*", "*tuyo, tuya…*"],
            ["his, her, its, your (usted), their", "*su, sus*", "*suyo, suya…*"],
            ["our", "*nuestro, nuestra, nuestros, nuestras*", "*nuestro…*"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "examples",
          "items": [
            { "fr": "{Mis} padres viven en Texas.", "tr": "My parents live in Texas." },
            { "fr": "{Nuestra} casa es pequeña.", "tr": "Our house is small." },
            { "fr": "¿Es tu bolsa? — Sí, es {mía}.", "tr": "Is it your bag? — Yes, it's mine." },
            { "fr": "Es la casa de Ana. = Es {su} casa.", "tr": "It's Ana's house. = It's her house." }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "tip",
          "text": "No apostrophe-s in Spanish: «Ana's house» is *la casa {de} Ana*."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exercises": [
